77.The Commission shall have the power to providelegal representation to any informer, whistleblower or witnessduring an investigation, including inquiries at Magistrate’sCourt, without prejudice to such investigations and at a trialin the High Court into an alleged offence committed againstsuch whistleblower or witness in terms of sections 73, 74 and75 of this Act.

PART II

DECLARATION OF ASSETS AND LIABILITIES

79.Subject to section 2 of this Act, the objects of thisPart shall be to –

(a)compel all public officials to make periodicdeclarations of their assets and liabilities within andoutside Sri Lanka;

(b)provide for a centralized electronic system forsubmission of such declarations;

Protection ofwitnesses andpersonsassisting theCommissionandprovidinglegalrepresentationwherenecessary

Protection ofvictims’rights

Objects of

this Part

